# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-2: `Notes` is on the party's own bar in both of the adventuring
# screen's modes, and nothing else on either screen is the seam's.
#
# The two bars are two strings in two places — the 3D view's and the area
# map's — and the splice is a separate pair of points for each (#221), so
# one of them working says nothing about the other. `A` is the game's own
# AREA command and swaps between them; both runs receive it, which is
# what lets this be a pair leg at all.
about Notes is on the 3D bar and on the area bar, and nowhere else
kind pair
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel
# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), and both
# sides of this pair drive past the challenge, so both need it. Pinned
# by digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 260000000
every 25
# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because claiming a
# keystroke changes when the program does its own next repaint by less
# than the gap between two stills. One dump of slack, measured (#234).
slack 1

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
key A@10600

rect notes 273,192,311,199
rect bar 0,190,319,199

allow 0-9000 none
# The 3D view's bar: the difference is the six cells at its end.
allow 9025-10599 notes
# The swap itself redraws the whole screen and the two runs do it a few
# frames apart, so the frames it takes are named by nobody. What matters
# is on either side of it.
#
# The area map's bar: its own words are a different length, so where the
# splice falls is its own question and the assertion here is the row.
# Measuring that word's exact cells is what the sheet is for, and it is
# RDR-13's kind of question rather than this one.
allow 11200-end bar
